Chris Saunderson wrote:

> Hi,
>
> I've managed to get almost all the way through installing 5.0 Redhat
> on my AlphaStation 200, but now I'm getting the following prompt:
>
> "Pleae insert your boot disk in your first drive if it's not there
> already".
> ...

The expected diskette is the corresponding kernel image. It contains a
extended file system with a kernel. To see what is happening use the
Alt-F? keys, that is:

    Alt-F2    Console with a shell
    Alt-F3    Low level errors related with the instalation
    Alt-F4    System messages

By looking at Alt-F3 you can see which is the mount command issued and the
corresponding error.

I guess that what is happening is that you are inserting the wrong
diskette. The one you need is under 'images/*.img' (probably
'avanti.img'). It is needed only to copy the kernel to the root partition.

In the 'Alt-F2' console (or in another linux machine) you can try to mount
the diskette, just to verify that it is OK. Once mounted you will see the
'vmlinux.gz' file and a mini-root file system.

Good luck!

--
