So, I finally got it working. There may still be a problem
with the CMOS RAM timer powering up in a weird state, but
the real problem (system clock running at 2X correct speed)
has been fixed. I called in an expert (Chris Kantarjiev)
who changed _KERNEL_HZ in /usr/src/linux/include/asm/param.h
to be 2048 (instead of 1024 as it was shipped). This
fixed it. 

Slowwwwly I'm learning.






