   >
   > p.s. How people open up PPP conection in Linux? Do you use "usernet" and
   > hit the bar?
   >
     The serial port is _not_ standard... it's both ports put into one......
   you'll have to find a pinout and either make a spitter cable or get one
   somewhere....... deep in the archives of digital there is a page with the
   pinout.....I've seen it somewhere a long time ago, but I don't remember

Not entirely true. The Y splitter cable is only necessary if you want
to use COM2. COM1 works fine with a standard serial cable.

As to the original problem:

1) The default port speed for COM1 (/dev/cua0 or /dev/ttyS0) is 38400.
   If you don't configure the PPP dialer to also use that speed, you
   won't even get the modem to dial. If using setserial to change this
   speed, be sure to set the dialer to match.

2) The original PPP RPM on the RedHat 5.0 distribution was buggy.
   It is listed on the errata page, with a pointer to the fix. Go to:

      ftp://ftp.redhat.com/updates/5.0/alpha/ppp-2.3.3-2.alpha.rpm

Luck!

MarkG
