In article <#GUq0SHQ9GA.262@upnetnews04>, Zheng Hu wrote:
>After installed Linux 5.0 on a Dec Multia and tried to run X-windows, I got
>a Fatal server error
>(--) DEC_TGA: MemBase needed for TGA support    --- check /proc/pci for base
>address.
>
>I will be back at the root prompt.  I stalled everything according to
>instruction and loaded Unlisted Card, and TGA xserver.  Please help!!
>

RedHat hasn't picked this up in their errata yet??

Ok, take a look at /proc/pci (cat /proc/pci, you'll likely need to be
root for this).  Somewhere in the listing you will see a reference to
the TGA video adapter, giving its memory base address.  On my UDB it
was 0x0a000000, IIRC.

Edit /etc/X11/lib/X11/XF86Config.  Find the stanza dealing with
accelerated video adapters, and insert the line:

Membase 0xxxxxxx

using the address found in /proc/pci.

This is being written from memory, as I'm not in front of the machine
at the moment, but hopefully will get you going.

Steve




