Patrick Theato  <theato@micky.zdv.Uni-Mainz.DE> wrote:
>On Thu, 19 Feb 1998, Ron Trolard wrote:
>
>>   The serial port is _not_ standard... it's both ports put into one......
>> you'll have to find a pinout and either make a spitter cable or get one
>> somewhere....... deep in the archives of digital there is a page with the
>> pinout.....I've seen it somewhere a long time ago, but I don't remember
>
>Are you sure ?
>
>My modem works fine without any splitter cable. I just just a standard
>cable. I did nothing special on my multia. But I also have no idea, why it
>shouldn't work.

You're both right.

The Multia puts two serial ports on a single DB25, but the pinouts of
the first serial port exactly match those for a standard, single
serial port on a DB25.

Without the splitter, you can only access ttyS0, but if you get the
cable, you've suddenly got ttyS1 as well.

There is enough information on various web pages to build the cable
yourself.
