RS-232 has specified a second serial port on the 25 pin connector for years
(what did you think all of those extra pins were for?) I've added the
corresponding 9 pin D assignments. The manual says the serial port pinout is:

Port A        PC 9 Pin Equiv.

2    TXD        3
3    RXD        2
4    RTS        7
5    CTS        8
6    DSR        6
7    GND        5
8    DCD        1
20    DTR        4
22    RI        9

Port B

14    TXD_2        3
16    RXD_2        2
19    RTS_2        7
13   CTS_2        8
23    DSR_2        6
(use same ground as port 1)
7    GND         5
12   DCD_2        1
11    DTR_2        4
25    RI_2        9

FWIW, DEC still sells the manual for the Multia for about $80.  It's not really
