COPY-PASTE -----------------------------
How do I build the Alpha kernel ?

As usual, and as specified in the kernel's README. Just don't forget these three
points if you are used to Linux/Intel :

       Edit the main Makefile and replace ARCH=i386 with ARCH=alpha.
       Use make boot, instead of make zImage, to build the kernel (don't strip
vmlinux yourself after a make zImage : one believes it works but in
       fact the module symbol table is unwantedly removed).
       Your compiled kernel will be found in
/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz; unlike on the Intel platform, it is
merely a gzip of
       the stripped object file.
------------------------------------------------------
