>would like to be assured, that linux will work on it (I don't want to
>dirty my hands with WinNT). Can anyone tell me, if merging this
>hardware and linux will be successful?

Yes, it'll work nicely, there are no peculiarities that I've noticed with
the AXPpci board. As with any alpha running Linux though, you'll probably
notice that some software won't work correctly due to assumptions about
32bit pointers, etc. But RedHat installs and works ok.

Also note that you'll need 36bit ECC RAM for the board to work. Those are
getting a bit hard to find these days. (At least in Sweden, everyone's
buying 32bit EDO ram or SDRAM these days)
If you haven't found it yet, there's some documentation available on
gatekeeper.dec.com in /pub/DEC/axppci

And don't pay too much, as someone already said, it's not esp. fast, about as
a P100/P133 or so.
Of course, the ability to tell your friends that you have an alpha might
be worth something.. :-)

/stefan

