I have seen this question many times now. Should this be in the FAQ?
AFAIK, DEC compiler gives the best performance, about a factor of three
better than egcs-g77 for floating point intensive calculations, (with
nearly factor of two coming from its math library, dxml). Since DEC does
not have a compiler for Linux, you need to compile your programs on a
Digital Unix machine, statically linked, and run it on the Linux machine.
This achieves the best performance compared to any other compilers,
commercial or not.

I have seen a petition someone sent to Digital to sell their compilers
on the Linux platform. It would help if more people are asking them.

Xiaoguang Zhang

