Hmmm ... usually only the MIPS-based systems from DEC are called DECstations ?

The old TurboChannel based Alphas (3000/300,/400,/500,/600,/700) are
not supported by Linux/Alpha so far. We are currently working on Turbo-
Channel support for the MIPS based DECstations (see 
http://decstation.unix-ag.org) which might also be of use for the TC Alphas.
The I/O ASIC used in the Personal DECstation 5000/xx and DECstation 5000/1xx
is also rumoured to be identical to the one used in these Alphas.

There is rudimentary support from NetBSD (http://www.netbsd.org) for the
old Alphas, but this doesn't support graphics console so far, IIRC.

For more information on the TurboChannel Alphas, you can find the 
System Programmer's Reference from DEC on decstation.unix-ag.org. This should
be a fairly complete reference for Linux porters ...

Now, if someone gave me a TurboChannel Alpha ....

