Very far from it.  There is a HUGE difference between "naively compiled"
blas version generally available from netlib and carefuly optimized libraries
which implement the same functions for a specific processor.  Linux
on Alpha undboubtely can use a work in this are but this is not likely
to happen until some vitaly interested parties sit down and put an effort
and time to it.

One does not have to start such effort entirely from scratch.  Something
was done already.  Here are some URLs to consult:

Fast GEMM:
ftp://ftp.enseeiht.fr/pub/numerique/BLAS/RISC/
Implementation for Linux/Alpha but with docs in Japanese:
ftp.eni.co.jp/.2/Linux-Alpha-JP/ftp.statabo.rim.or.jp/BLAS/libdgemm-980110.tar.gz
General BLAS issues for a specific processor:
http://www.kachinatech.com/~hjjou/scilib/opt_blas.html
http://www.kachinatech.com/~hjjou/scilib/phipac.html

   Happy Hacking,
