Hello all,

I have a AlphaStation 400 (Avanti) with a DE500 BA (21143) ethernet card.
I have successfully configured the card on Linux-Intel to operate at
100Mb/full duplex with versions 0.83 and 0.87 of Donald Becker's
amazing tulip.c driver (thank you Mr. Becker).  I could not, however,
use this driver with kernel 2.0.33 (or other 2.1.x kernels) on the Alpha
because of unaligned trap errors.

In v0.534 of de4x5.c, davies@maniac.ultranet.com identified the issue 
as such:

     I have removed the buffer copies needed for receive on Intels.  I
     cannot remove them for   Alphas since  the  Tulip hardware only does
     longword aligned  DMA transfers  and  the  Alphas get alignment
     traps with  non longword aligned data copies (which makes them really
     slow). No comment.    

The Digital DE500 BA 21143 card seems to function with v0.534 version
of de4x5.c under kernel 2.0.33 without any unaligned trap errors, but I 
cannot get it to operate at 100Mb/full duplex.  Could anyone suggest a
solution where I could either avoid the unaligned trap errors I have
received with the tulip driver or get the de4x5 driver to support 100Mb?  


Thank you for your time.

-David



