Hello:

I posted an article in comp.os.linux.alpha, comp.os.linux.misc looking for
advice on Linux distributions for the Alpha computing platform.  As is
my usual practice, I "munged" my "From:" and "Reply-To:" headers to avoid
receiving spam.

A user at a small Linux site in Germany (Kai Dupke, aka <dupke@koma.han.de>)
for, whatever reason, took it upon himself to send a message to my
postmaster complaining about my "noncomformance with RFC" protocols.
My postmaster passed it along to me, probably just as confused as I was!

I know a lot of Linux users, not to mention a lot of other USENET posters
engage in this kind of self-preservation (I'm not exactly thrilled with
having to resort to it myself, but...) and I don't need this kind of
harrassment (I get enough revenge spam) so I wanted to give a heads-up and
to find out what others thought of Kai's actions.

Here is a message I fired off to him:

From 3srf@qlink.queensu.ca Mon Feb  9 09:31:46 1998
Date: Mon, 9 Feb 1998 09:31:05 -0500 (EST)
