Rolf Hemmerling <hemmerling@geocities.com> wrote in article
<34DF5996.10F1AA3D@geocities.com>...
> Where are the *sources* of the terminal definition files of
> TERMINFO ? The compiled binaries are usually in sub-directories
> below

You can "decompile" the terminfo files using the infocmp utility, it will
give back the source format for the desired term type.  For example:

	infocmp -I wyse50

returns the source code for the Wyse50 terminal type in something that
could be modified, then compiled using the tic utility.  There are
utilities in the family to convert between termcap and terminfo.  You
should probably check the man pages for more info, I haven't used this set
of utilities very much.

					Jay



