[what RAM works in a UDB/Multia]
>That's NOT true, just a normal 72pin non-EDO wouldn't work, It must be a
>true ECC type!

Any 72-pin 60 NS _true parity_ RAM will work.  It doesn't need to be any
special kind of "ECC" RAM, but it must have hardware parity; "logic parity"
SIMMS such as are sometimes sold will not work.

One source I've had good experience with is Einstein's Computer:
http://www.esc-tech.com/

