I've been running RH4.2 for a year in a AlphaStation 255/300 with both Linux
and OpenVMS  without any problem (I need the second one for some customers).
Now I'm about to upgrade to RH5.0.

As I have just the SRM console I boot MILO from diskette with '>>> boot dva'
and
then Linux with MILO's commands.

The MILO I use comes from:

ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Miniloader/v2.0/2.0.22/XL-avanti/milo.dd

It's a very old version, so you can probably get a better one from

... Miniloader/v2.0/latest/AlphaStation 255/milo.dd

at the same site.

By "better" I mean that the device drivers and improvements introduced in new
kernels
automatically becomes a part of MILO. This doesn't mean that you have to run
the same
kernel than MILO, but rather that if you can boot with a MILO version you can

successfully run the same kernel version.

I hope this helps. Please contact me if you have further questions. Good
luck!

--
