I don't think anyone's mentioned the 'init=' kernel parameter.  To
totally bypass init, do something similar to the following (make sure
whatever you execute is statically linked!):
	boot sdb4:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sdb4 init=/bin/ash.static

Once up you'll have to (re)mount the various files systems by hand, of
course, and to shut down you'll need to unmount everything (or remount
'em read-only) and hit the BRS.

